ign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-\\frac{1}{3})$ | $(-\\frac{1}{3},0)$ | $(0,3)$ | $(3,4)$ | $(4,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $(4-x)^{2}$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $3x+1$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x-3$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the inequality $f(x)<0,$ we look at the bottom row to determine where $f(x)$ is negative.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)$ is negative on the intervals $(-\\frac{1}{3},0)$ and $(0,3)$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $f(x)<0$ for all $x\\in (-\\frac{1}{3},0)⋃(0,3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281503 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c880562-074d-593c-b7dc-80bb39499fb1" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Polynomial Inequality when the Right-Hand Side is Nonzero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83970429-32b0-54f2-9534-32f6390fd0ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281505}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83970429-32b0-54f2-9534-32f6390fd0ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281505} :answer-field/id #uuid "42952ef4-7093-5cde-ba0b-bfc334794ffe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281504} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23dbdbe9-e80c-519c-bbf1-fc073df6ce3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281507}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23dbdbe9-e80c-519c-bbf1-fc073df6ce3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281507} :answer-field/id #uuid "1124a1b7-13f0-5f69-a047-8e102ebf8e8e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186