$f(x)$ is negative.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)$ is negative on the intervals $(-3,0)$ and $(0,3).$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $f(x)<0$ for all $x\\in (-3,0)\\cup (0,3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281510 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c80b75e7-19b2-534b-97f8-aba563ebe058" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Factored Cubic Polynomial Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd13aeea-205c-522f-9233-efc273a7b981" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd13aeea-205c-522f-9233-efc273a7b981" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281512} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac4b4f6b-658b-57ab-b594-71d61f2e1047" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281511} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50141ea6-2b82-5cc2-a134-edb987e612b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50141ea6-2b82-5cc2-a134-edb987e612b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281514} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9d38c0d-4e77-5eaa-b300-1e330bd731ab" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281513} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2270b006-1b3a-5ac6-b9b4-e2bc904aef89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2270b006-1b3a-5ac6-b9b4-e2bc904aef89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281516} :answer-field/id #uuid "0068ae67-ebee-58d6-943e-39944bf1d694" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281515}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9188f3a2-712f-55e9-9776-09ed97c41357" :question/math-academy-id "q-281473" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $(3x-4)(1-x)(x+2)>0.$\n\n$x\\in $\n$(-\\infty ,$\n{{field-1}}$)⋃\\,($\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we define the function $f(x)$ as\n\n$$\nf(x)=(3x-4)(1-x)(x+2).\n$$\n\nSo we're now solving the inequality $f(x)>0.$\n\nThe solutions to the equation $f(x)=0$ are $x=-2,$ $x=1,$ and $x=\\frac{4}{3}.$ These roots divide the number line into $4$ subintervals: \n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,-2),\\,(-2,1),\\,(1,\\frac{4}{3}),\\,(\\frac{4}{3},\\infty )\n$$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of the intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-2)$ | $(-2,1)$ | $(1,\\frac{4}{3})$ | $(\\frac{4}{3},\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3x-4$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $1-x$ | $+$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| $x+2$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the inequality $f(x)>0,$ we look at the bottom row to determine where $f(x)$ is positive.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)$ is positive on the intervals $(-\\infty ,-2)$ and $(1,\\frac{4}{3}).$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that $f(x)>0$ for all $x\\in (-\\infty ,-2)⋃(1,\\frac{4}{3}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281517 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e675f1c-9093-5f6e-a3b3-112d0bc8e516" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Factored Higher-Order Polynomial Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef0fd3da-4bcc-580f-9520-2103edda3948" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef0fd3da-4bcc-580f-9520-2103edda3948" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281519} :answer-field/id #uuid "3763c812-8394-5bca-ab1c-03bc9b2afd04" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281518} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47a99f58-0448-5015-b75a-eded02f92b04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47a99f58-0448-5015-b75a-eded02f92b04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281521} :answer-field/id #uuid "af0d074d-74d6-5752-a019-303611cc6656" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281520} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69b7249a-16fa-5540-904f-8d01d1480e5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281523}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69b7249a-16fa-5540-904f-8d01d1480e5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281523} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a7004e6-e8c1-501b-a3c9-37ffba035fcf" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281522} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d97192e6-52b9-5ea3-8f10-627b35aae4ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d97192e6-52b9-5ea3-8f10-627b35aae4ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281525} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0b96cc7-03ed-5117-bcc5-6752111327fb" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281524} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4ccd6a8-ba78-5be9-9934-41e040349d5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4ccd6a8-ba78-5be9-9934-41e040349d5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281527} :answer-field/id #uuid "583285c3-76ae-53c4-9c33-ffad834c7472" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "60797e40-438b-5570-8a95-24ee19d3022e" :question/math-academy-id "q-281704" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $(x+2)(2x-1)(1-x)(3x-4)(x-5)\\le 0.$\n\n$x\\in [$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$]⋃\\,[$\n{{field-3}}$,$\n{{field-4}}$]⋃\\,[$\n{{field-5}}$,\\infty )$" :question/worked-solution "First, we define the function $f(x)$ as\n\n$$\nf(x)=(x+2)(2x-1)(1-x)(3x-4)(x-5).\n$$\n\nSo we're now solving the inequality $f(x)\\le 0.$\n\nThe solutions to the equation $f(x)=0$ are $x=-2,$ $x=\\frac{1}{2},$ $x=1,$ $x=\\frac{4}{3},$ and $x=5.$ These roots divide the number line into $6$ subintervals:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,-2),\\,(-2,\\frac{1}{2}),\\,(\\frac{1}{2},1),\\,(1,\\frac{4}{3}),\\,(\\frac{4}{3},5),\\,(5,\\infty )\n$$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of the intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-2)$ | $(-2,\\frac{1}{2})$ | $(\\frac{1}{2},1)$ | $(1,\\frac{4}{3})$ | $(\\frac{4}{3},5)$ | $(5,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2x-1$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $1-x$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| $x+2$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $3x-4$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x-5$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the inequality $f(x)\\le 0,$ we look at the bottom row to determine where $f(x)$ is negative.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)\\le 0$ on the intervals $(-2,\\frac{1}{2})$, $(1,\\frac{4}{3})$, and $(5,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, remembering that the roots are also solutions, we conclude that $f(x)\\le 0$ for all $x\\in [-2,\\frac{1}{2}]⋃[1,\\frac{4}{3}]⋃[5,\\infty ).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281528 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e675f1c-9093-5f6e-a3b3-112d0bc8e516" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Factored Higher-Order Polynomial Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "188e62fd-bcd1-515a-8207-c1117a4b8b65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "188e62fd-bcd1-515a-8207-c1117a4b8b65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281530} :answer-field/id #uuid "9de28166-112d-518d-b5b6-b0cbb728e0ac" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281529} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14dbbfa6-dab4-5569-84e5-58a5ee903d80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14dbbfa6-dab4-5569-84e5-58a5ee903d80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281532} :answer-field/id #uuid "c203be72-1752-5ca2-ab60-aa25ca1d31e0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281531} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72683dbe-cf0f-582b-baee-87854a8639b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72683dbe-cf0f-582b-baee-87854a8639b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281534} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3cae0d2-51a5-5ad4-87ee-e837d408487b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281533}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "01fdc9a5-492f-5aee-bfa0-e1d7b2a5216c" :question/math-academy-id "q-281717" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $(3x-1)^{2}(2x+5)^{2}(4-x)(x-2)\\ge 0.$\n\n$x\\in $\n${-\\frac{5}{2},$\n{{field-1}}\n$}⋃$\n$[$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}$]$" :question/worked-solution "First, we define the function $f(x)$ as\n\n$$\nf(x)=(3x-1)^{2}(2x+5)^{2}(4-x)(x-2).\n$$\n\nSo we're now solving the inequality $f(x)\\ge 0.$\n\nThe solutions to the equation $f(x)=0$ are $x=-\\frac{5}{2},\\text{ }\\frac{1}{3},\\text{ }2,$ and $4.$ These roots divide the number line into five subintervals:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,-\\frac{5}{2}),\\,(-\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{1}{3}),\\,(\\frac{1}{3},2),\\,(2,4),\\,(4,\\infty )\n$$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of the intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-\\frac{5}{2})$ | $(-\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{1}{3})$ | $(\\frac{1}{3},2)$ | $(2,4)$ | $(4,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $(3x-1)^{2}$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $(2x+5)^{2}$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $(4-x)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| $(x-2)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the inequality $f(x)\\ge 0,$ we look at the bottom row to determine where $f(x)$ is positive.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)$ is non-negative only on the closed interval $(2,4).$\n\nTherefore, remembering that the roots are also solutions, we conclude that $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in {-\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{1}{3}}⋃[2,4].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281535 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6bea8139-82a8-5c0a-9d3b-f3a47356773e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Expanded 